                                        <div class="tab-pane fade active show" id="pills-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Objectives"><p align="justify">The School of Engineering and Technology has the responsibility of initiating academic, continuing and extension education programmes in the areas of engineering and technology. The School has developed several programmes aimed at increasing job potential and economic advantage to the learners. To fulfill its mandate, the School regularly interacts with employing agencies, professional bodies and industry so as to reflect educational and training needs of the targeted learner group in the curriculum. The School practices participative and collaborative strategy by inviting different industries.</p>
<p align="justify">The Programmes launched by the School range from a competency bases non-credit vocational qualification certificate to doctoral degree in engineering and technology. The school had successfully launched its programmes at various levels in the areas of Civil Engineering, Mechanical Engineering and Electrical Engineering and also in the area of Renewable Energy.</p>
<p align="justify"><b>Vision:</b> The School of Engineering and Technology(SOET) aims to create a conducive learning environment and expertise in state of the art technologies, vocations and professions at all levels fulfilling the nation’s need of employment generations, skill upgradation, continuing education, research and development, using innovative technologies and methodologies, networking with technical and professional institutions and industries.</p>
<p align="justify"><b>Mission:</b> To develop education work linkages and provide opportunities by disseminating knowledge and skills in employment oriented technical, vocational and professional education at all levels of learning so as to reach the rural and urban masses through distance, blended and other modes of learning using various information and communication technologies.</p></div>

                                        
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="History"  ><p align="text">The School of Engineering & Technology (SOET), came into existence in 1987, with a clear mandate to address the issues pertaining to continuing and extension education requirements in the country. The School devises and conducts academic continuing and extension education programmes in engineering and technology areas for disadvantaged and economically weaker sections, ranging from certificate to diploma/degree aimed at increasing job potential,knowledge and skill enhancement of learners. SOET also provides skill Upgradation and Training for capacity building using innovative technologies and methodology.</p>

</div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-3" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Director&#39;sMessage"  ><p>It is my privilege to welcome you to the School of Engineering and Technology (SOET) at the Indira Gandhi National Open University (IGNOU). Since its inception in 1989, SOET has remained steadfast in its mission to expand access to high-quality technical and professional education through innovative, flexible, and industry-relevant programmes.</p>
<p>The School today offers a broad spectrum of programmes ranging from vocational certificates to postgraduate degrees and professional qualifications. Our academic offerings include the B.Sc. in Applied Science & Energy, M.Sc. in Renewable Energy and Environment, M.Sc. in Industrial Safety, MBA in Logistics and Supply Chain Management, and MBA in Construction Management. We also provide specialised programmes such as the Diploma in Smart City Development and Management, PG Certificate in Inventory Planning & Warehousing, Certificate in Waste Water Treatment Techniques, Certificate in Condition Monitoring, Certificate in Energy & Technology Management, Advanced Certificate in Power Distribution, and Competency Certificate in Power Distribution.</p>
<p>In addition to these programmes, SOET focuses on the major disciplines of Civil, Mechanical, Electrical Engineering, Architecture, and the rapidly growing area of Renewable Energy. This multidisciplinary approach ensures that learners are equipped not only with domain-specific knowledge but also with the skills to address emerging challenges in sustainable development, infrastructure, and technology-driven industries.</p>
<p>Our strength lies in our continuous engagement with industries, professional bodies, and employing agencies, which allows us to design curricula that are contemporary, skill-oriented, and aligned with workforce needs. By leveraging distance and blended learning approaches and the power of information and communication technologies, SOET is able to reach learners in both urban and rural areas, fulfilling IGNOU’s mission of inclusive education.</p>
<p>We remain committed to nurturing talent, fostering innovation, and contributing to national development by preparing professionals who can lead with knowledge, creativity, and purpose.</p>
<p>Director, SOET</p></div>
